==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|flexus}}, past participle of {{m|la|flecto||to bend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/flɛks/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-flex.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛks|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|flecks}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[flexibility|Flexibility]], [[pliancy]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} An act of [[flexing]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Gary Noy|title=Red Dirt: A Journey of Discovery in the Landscape of Imagination, California's Gold Country|publisher=iUniverse|isbn=9780595222766|page=144
|passage=The hills become more rounded. The slopes are either the stooped shoulders of an aging colossus or the muscular '''flexes''' of a geologic youngster, but they are pleasant, comforting. This landscape is what most would think of {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|chiefly|UK|Irish}} Any flexible [[insulated]] [[electrical]] [[wiring]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} A flexible [[insulated]] [[electrical]] [[cord]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1950|author=Norman Lindsay|authorlink=Norman Lindsay|title={{w|Dust or Polish?}}|publisher=Angus and Robertson|location=Sydney|page=57|passage=The books lent her by Dr Grimble on period furniture and ceramics interested her deeply, and she studied them at night in the silence of the shop, where she had a '''flex''' and a reading lamp installed at her own expense.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Flexible [[ductwork]], typically flexible plastic over a metal wire coil to shape a tube.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Aaron Lubeck|title=Green Restorations: Sustainable Building and Historic Homes|page=221
|passage='''Flex''' is quick and cheaper to install than metallic systems, but it yields higher pressure loss than other types of ducts and requires runs of less than 15 feet, minimal turns and elimination of kinks.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|geometry}} A [[point of inflection]].
# {{senseid|en|act or instance of flaunting}} {{lb|en|countable|slang}} The act or an instance of [[flaunt]]ing something; something one considers [[impressive]].
#* '''2017''', "Mogul Bites", ''Black American Moguls'', Fall 2017, [https://issuu.com/mogulsmagazine/docs/black_amer_moguls_fall_2017_issue page 6]:
#*: Getting together with other power players at Masa is the ultimate '''flex''' of conspicuous consumption. {{...}} A party of five or more requires a deposit of $200 per person at least one week prior to the reservation.
#* '''2019''', Seth Sommerfeld, "Worldwide Web", ''Inlander'', 4 July 2019 - 10 July 2019, [https://issuu.com/theinlander/docs/inlander_07-04-2019 page 37]:
#*: It's an achievement to stand out from other Marvel movies in terms of special effects, but this whole movie feels like a '''flex''' for those computer wizards.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Daniel Varghese|title=Aesop's Hand Sanitizer Is a '''Flex''' for an Anxious Time|titleurl=https://www.gq.com/story/aesops-hand-sanitizer-coronavirus|journal=GQ|date=6 March 2020}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}

